.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="There is exactly one polynomial of degree \leq n through n+1 distinct points, so LagrangeInterpolant and NewtonDividedDifference -- built from completely different representations (a sum of basis polynomials vs. nested divided differences) -- must produce identical curves. Both are also exact for any polynomial up to the interpolation degree, which this script verifies directly.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/numerical_analysis/interpolation/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_01_lagrange_newton_thumb.png
    :alt:

